QuestGuidance.Register("en",35,{
[1089]="70057D91\n1\tTalk to Maud Tatter\030Collect fine clay (total: 6)\030Collect cut pine logs (total: 6)\030Collect willow boughs (total: 3)\tClay can be found on the banks of the pond north west of Bree. Willow sprays can be collected near a pond south of Bree. Cut pine wood can be found outside of Bree. Fine lace can be procured from the tailor Maud Tatter in Bree. Rona Turner has asked you to collect clay, willow sprays, firewood, and fine lace.\n2\tReturn to Rona Turner\tRona Turner is located in Bree. Bring the materials to Rona Turner.\n",
[1090]="70041366\n1\tRetrieve Turthoren's keys\tTurthoren's keys are on a half-troll in Tungobel. Retrieve the keys for Turthoren.\n2\tLock doors in Tungobel (total: 8)\tEach home in Tungobel has an unlocked door. Lock each door in Tungobel.\n3\tReturn the keys to Turthoren\tTurthoren is near the village of Tungobel. Return the keys to Turthoren.\n",
[1091]="7006C53D\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Sar-kidul (total: 12)\tYour mission is to take the fight to the Orcs in Sar-kidul and eliminate them.\n2\tFind and defeat Madmurúk\tFind and defeat Madmurúk in Sar-kidul.\n",
[1092]="70026196\n1\tTalk to Orchalwë at Tinnudir\tOrchalwë is at Tinnudir. Orchalwë will be pleased to hear the western shores of Evendim are safe.\n",
[1093]="7003A632\n1\tTravel to Aldburg\tAldburg is west of Beaconwatch. Cútha told you to return to Aldburg and let Arcil know of your victory against the Boar-tribe.\n2\tTalk to Arcil\tThane Arcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg. Thane Cútha told you to return to Aldburg and speak with Thane Arcil.\n",
[1094]="7000F1DD\n1\tDefeat Laulu-vihâja and collect his guts\tBurgthryth has asked you to retrieve the guts of the kalpa-kita, Laulu-vihâja, from which she will make new strings for her lute. Laulu-vihâja is on Kissa-sari, South-west from Jänis-leiri.\n2\tCollect Cat-gut\tBurgthryth has asked you to retrieve the guts of the kalpa-kita, Laulu-vihâja, from which she will make new strings for her lute. Laulu-vihâja is on Kissa-sari, South-west from Jänis-leiri.\n3\tBring the cat-gut to Burgthryth in Jänis-leiri\tHaving retrieved a pile of cat-gut from the very kalpa-kita that wrecked Burgthryth's lute, you should return it to her as quickly as possible. Burgthryth is at Jänis-leiri.\n",
[1095]="7006AB61\n1\tRecover treasure caches (total: 8)\tKhôltekh has asked that you return any valuables you see in Deshûkh, the Blood Market to him, so that he may return them to the families from which they were stolen. Deshûkh is located in Dil-irmíz, south-east of Mekab-kuphâr.\n2\tReturn to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.\n",
[1096]="70065AA4\n1\tFind the vegetable sack's rightful owner in Glaniath\tYou have found a sack of vegetables that were stolen by Corsairs at Hárba's Camp. You should venture north to Glaniath to see if you can return these vegetables to their rightful owner.\n2\tTalk to Annaben\tAnnaben in Glaniath seems to be in the process of transporting sacks full of vegetables. The sack you found in Hárba's Camp may have belonged to her. You should talk to her.\n",
[1097]="7002F98A\n1\tConvince Hwitmon to allow Inhild to visit Randgar's farm\tHwitmon resides at his estate, just east of the central fountain in Cliving, with his daughter. Inhild would like her father's permission to visit Randgar's farm one last time to see what yet remains and to say farewell.\n2\tEscort Inhild to Randgar's farm to say good-bye\tRandgar's farm lies south of Cliving, along the road to the east. Inhild has been allowed to visit Randgar's farm in order to say farewell to the man she loved.\n3\tSpeak to Hwitmon\tHwitmon resides at his estate, just east of the central fountain in Cliving. Inhild and Randgar have asked that Hwitmon not be told the truth, as he would be happiest to believe that his daughter is with a wealthy man in Edoras.\n",
[1098]="7006C4E6\n1\tSpeak with the wealthy merchant, Igbâl at his home in Jirush\tSigênik instructed you to meet each of the elders of Jirush, and to pay special attention to their greetings. One among them, the elder directly supporting the rebels, will greet you differently. The first elder to meet is the wealthy merchant, Igbâl south and east of Sigênik.\n2\tSpeak with Igbâl's translator, Galamê\tIgbâl would not speak with you. His translator suggested you speak with him instead. He stands very near Igbâl within Igbâl's home.\n3\tSpeak with the Elder Zealot, Zidemel\tWith your introduction to Igbâl concluded you should seek Elder Zidemel. He is a zealot who can be found tending a flock of adherent in the outpost. He preaches near the fountain in the outpost mall.\n4\tSpeak with the Elder Carpenter, Nangar\tYou met with the Elder Zealot Zidemel. You should now turn your attention to find the elder Nangar. He is the outpost's main caretaker. He lives at a home south-west of the northern entrance to Jirush.\n5\tSpeak with the Elder Hunter, Malgat\tYou met with Nangar. Something about the meeting was different than it was with the others. What was it? You should think about that as you prepare to meet Malgat at his home east of first free standing arch from the northern entrance of Jirush.\n6\tReturn to Sigênik near the north entrance at Jirush\tYou met with the four elders and introduced yourself as Sigênik instructed. Now that you are known to the Elders of Jirush. Return to Sigênik near the northern entrance to Jirush. He will likely prepare you for your test.\n",
[1099]="700080F1\n1\tTalk to Elsie Woodruff\tElsie Woodruff is in Trestlebridge. While Mattie and Noll fix the cart and load it with the lumber they've collected, Mattie asked you to go back to Trestlebridge and tell his wife that he's safe.\n",
[1100]="7000782D\n1\tCollect the bucket\tStaddle's well is north and west of the Silverwater Spring. Willowsong told you to return the bucket of water to Staddle's well.\n2\tTalk to Longo Daegmund by the Staddle Town Well\tLongo is standing by the well in the town square of Staddle. You did as Willowsong instructed. Tell Longo Daegmund that the well should be safe to drink from again.\n",
[1101]="70028235\n1\tTalk to Haul at Echad Naeglanc\tEchad Naeglanc lies to the south and east of Bledhun's camp. Bledhun has asked you to warn his allies regarding the evil ones who dwell in the Bonevales.\n",
[1102]="7001567B\n1\tCarefully arm the traps (total: 6)\tThe traps are in the southern halls of Zelem-melek, to the west and north of the Orc-watch. The dwarves placed them near Gabil-mamach and Budkhul-tharâkh. You should arm the traps that have stopped working to help make the passages safer against the enemies of Khazad-dûm.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have armed the traps meant to hinder the advance of the Ghâsh-hai in southern Zelem-melek. Though the dwarves know it not, you have rendered them a great service.\n",
[1103]="70071E97\n1\tReach Ally standing with the Hamât Renewed\tAs Hamât rises anew, you have proven an invaluable ally. Mizâdi and her agents look to you for further assistance. You should return to Mizâdi's encampment and treat with Lumgâna.\n2\tSpeak to Lumgâna at Mizâdi's encampment\tAs Hamât rises anew, you have proven an invaluable ally. Mizâdi and her agents look to you for further assistance. You should return to Mizâdi's encampment and treat with Lumgâna.\n",
[1104]="70057E65\n1\tTalk to Fróthi in Erebor\tFróthi can be found in Erebor. You should talk to Fróthi in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Léothred in Erebor\tLéothred can be found in Erebor. You should talk to Léothred in Erebor.\n3\tTravel to Skarháld\tFróthi can be found in Skarháld. You should talk to Fróthi in Skarháld.\n4\tTalk to Fróthi in Skarháld\tFróthi can be found in Skarháld. You should talk to Fróthi in Skarháld.\n5\tGather supplies in Skarháld (total: 6)\tSupplies can be found throughout Skarháld. You should gather supplies for Fróthi and Léothred.\n6\tBring the supplies to Léothred in Skarháld\tLéothred can be found in Skarháld. You should bring the supplies to Léothred in Skarháld.\n",
[1105]="70071E86\n1\tReach Ally standing with the Kintai of Sul Madásh\tYou honour the Kintai and assist them with the efforts to preserve Adagím. You should return to their settlement of Sul Madásh to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.\n2\tSpeak with Aralath at Sul Madásh\tYou honour the Kintai and assist them with the efforts to preserve Adagím. You should return to their settlement of Sul Madásh to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.\n",
[1106]="7006C96B\n1\tReach Ally tier with the Adúrhid\tYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.\n2\tVisit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a gift\tYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.\n",
[1107]="7006C971\n1\tReach Ally tier with the Ikorbâni\tYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.\n2\tVisit Kildûg at Iridír to claim a gift\tYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.\n",
[1108]="7006C963\n1\tReach Ally tier with the Phetêkari\tVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.\n2\tVisit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your gift\030Visit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh\tVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.\n",
[1109]="70071E94\n1\tReach Ally standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh\tYou stand by your agreement with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh and assist in the recovery of the broken land. You should return to Quartermaster Semanísi to see what acclaim your deeds have wrought.\n2\tSpeak with Semanísi at Jiret-menêsh\tYou stand by your agreement with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh and assist in the recovery of the broken land. You should return to Quartermaster Semanísi to see what acclaim your deeds have wrought.\n",
[1110]="70071E99\n1\tReach Ally standing with The City of Zajâna\tYou remain true to your word, aiding the City of Zajâna earnestly. You should return to the city to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.\n2\tSpeak with Alahamâr at Zajâna\tYou remain true to your word, aiding the City of Zajâna earnestly. You should return to the city to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.\n",
[1111]="70044D5B\n1\tSearch for Círgon near the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle\tThe Baths of Belecthor can be found to the north in the Fourth Circle. Mílien has asked you to seek out her son, Círgon, at the Baths of Belecthor near their home or below in Egalmoth's Green.\n2\tSearch for Círgon in Egalmoth's Green in the Third Circle\tEgalmoth's Green can be found to the north in the Third Circle. You were unable to find Círgon at the Baths and should now search Egalmoth's Green.\n",
[1112]="7001AF9A\n1\tTalk to Adso Haybank at his camp\tAdso's camp can be found west along the Great East Road between the gate of Bree and Buckland. Watcher Grimbriar sent you to assist Adso Haybank with solving the problems the hobbit currently has with the brigands out of the south.\n",
[1113]="7004CF83\n1\tDefeat corrupted Huorns (total: 2)\030Defeat corrupted bears (total: 4)\030Defeat corrupted wolves (total: 4)\030Defeat corrupted boars (total: 4)\030Defeat gloomwaters (total: 8)\tYou should patrol along the river Rhachló, looking out for any beasts corrupted by its waters.\n2\tMeet up with Oroniel\tOroniel has returned and can be found further south along the banks of the Rhachló. You should reconvene with Oroniel and discuss how next to proceed.\n",
[1114]="70017D71\n1\tFind the dwelling place of the Swamped One\030Defeat the Swamped One\tThe Swamped One can be found in the ruins of Harloeg, south-east of Ost Guruth. Mosco Mudbottom has asked you to deal with a Nameless creature that is rumoured to be lurking in southern Harloeg. Mosco mentioned that the Nameless will likely be near an old stone altar.\n2\tReturn to Mosco Mudbottom\tMosco Mudbottom is at Ost Guruth, north-west of Harloeg. Now that you have confronted and slain the Swamped One, return to Mosco Mudbottom and tell him of your success.\n",
[1115]="7004DA6F\n1\tTalk to Ambassador Spakorth before King Thorin III's throne\tAmbassador Spakorth can be found before King Thorin III's throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. Ambassador Spakorth has asked you to accompany him to address King Thorin in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. Ambassador Spakorth has thanked King Thorin III for his mercy and offered the services of the Stout-axes to Durin's Folk.\n",
[1116]="70043DEE\n1\tDestroy enemy supplies (total: 10)\tEnemy supplies can be found on the Eastern side of Osgiliath. You should destroy enemy supplies.\n2\tSpeak with Edenos\tEdenos is at the Palace of Eldacar. You should speak to Edenos.\n",
[1117]="70071778\n1\tTalk to Mêshaget\tBefore leaving Gadim-ûn to meet with the others for your attack, the dwarf Mêshaget wants to talk to you.\n2\tComplete Instance: Ambush at the Heights\tMêshaget wishes to join you for your assault on the Ordâkhai supply caravan. You should talk to Nabatínu at Gadim-ûn when you are ready to join them for the attack.\n3\tTalk to Nabatínu\tYou have successfully completed your attack on the Ordâkhai supply caravan. You should talk to Nabatínu about the results.\n",
[1118]="7004DA74\n1\tFind and heal injured Raft-elves (total: 6)\tInjured Raft-elves can be found along the Forest River between Felegoth and Loeglond. You should seek out the missing Raft-elves and tend to their wounds if needed.\n2\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr.\n",
[1119]="7005850D\n1\tAdvance with the dwarf army\tPrince Durin of the Longbeards is ready to lead the charge on Gundabad. You should advance with the dwarf army!\n2\tDefeat the Beasts of Slaughter\tGorgar's trap has been sprung, and you must now fight in his arena or perish. You should defeat Gorgar's Beasts of Slaughter.\n3\tDefeat Gorgar and Ránulur\tYou have defeated the beasts, but Gorgar now intends to fight you himself! You must now face Gorgar the Ruthless and Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs in the arena!\n",
[1120]="700584FC\n1\tAdvance with the dwarf army\tPrince Durin of the Longbeards is ready to lead the charge on Gundabad. You should advance with the dwarf army!\n2\tDefeat the Beasts of Slaughter\tGorgar's trap has been sprung, and you must now fight in his arena or perish. You should defeat Gorgar's Beasts of Slaughter.\n3\tDefeat Gorgar and Ránulur\tYou have defeated the beasts, but Gorgar now intends to fight you himself! You must now face Gorgar the Ruthless and Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs in the arena!\n",
})
